{
  "$comment": "The AI and search crawlers crawler-log-report.py counts in a site's access logs, and where each vendor publishes the IP addresses its crawler uses. A request that names a crawler in its user agent is only that crawler if it comes from one of those addresses; anyone can send the user-agent string. The script ships no addresses: they change weekly, so `--refresh-ranges` downloads each list from the vendor into the local data folder (workspace_root()/cache/crawler-ranges.json, with the date fetched), and that is the script's only network call. It sends nothing from the logs. Without a download every request is reported as unverified, never as genuine. tests/test_crawler_log_report.py checks every entry and fails 30 days before any review_by (DMP_TODAY=YYYY-MM-DD freezes today). Added in 3.41.0.",
  "schema": "lists: name -> {url, vendor, docs_url, verified_on, review_by}; crawlers: one row each {token (case-insensitive substring of the user agent), vendor, role (search | user | training | ads | agent | search-index), lists (names above; empty when the vendor publishes none), docs_url, verified_on, review_by}. Each list is JSON {creationTime, prefixes: [{ipv4Prefix | ipv6Prefix}]}, the format all of these vendors use.",
  "max_age_days": 14,
  "lists": {
    "openai-searchbot": {"url": "https://openai.com/searchbot.json", "vendor": "OpenAI", "docs_url": "https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/bots", "verified_on": "2026-10-29", "review_by": "2027-01-31"},
